# Children's Ministries architecture

This app belongs to New Fadama Seventh-day Adventist Church. It records children, guardians, classes, and Sabbath attendance. A child's school is a text field on the child. Classes are a fixed ladder from Pre-school through SHS 3, and active children move up one class when the academic year ends.

Keep the runtime to two Docker Compose services: `web` (Django) and `db` (PostgreSQL). Serve static files with WhiteNoise inside the Django container. Do not add Redis, Celery, Nginx, or a frontend container unless a requirement explicitly asks for that service.

Use Django templates and HTMX. Do not introduce a JavaScript framework or an API for the browser.

Sabbath is Saturday, in Africa/Accra. Attendance statuses are PRESENT and ABSENT. A Saturday with no attendance row is not recorded, and it does not count as absent. Calculate age from the date of birth. Deactivate children instead of deleting their attendance history.

Enforce ADMIN, COORDINATOR, and TEACHER permissions on the server with Django groups.
